      "content": "SP 80 SE              THE LEE                 THE LEE 4/90                                          Ship's Figurehead from                                               'Admiral Lord Howe '                                                to north of Pipers - -                                             II Ship's figurehead.  1860 from the 'Admiral Lord Howe', the last wooden-wall warship built for the Royal Navy.  Renamed 'Impregnable' as a training ship.  The ship was broken up in the 1920s, along with a sister ship 'Hindustan' and used to provide the timber framing for Liberty and Co.'s store in Regent Street.  The figurehead was removed to The Lee and set up adjacent to Pipers by the Liberty family circa. 1924.  Half length figure of Lord Howe in admiral's uniform on Scroll from prow of ship.  Painted timber. Listing NGR: SP8999903920"
    }
